# Planned ON a 5560U INSIDE the Sigmond Proxmox VM (AI6VN-PM, VM 100:
# 10 vCPUs pinned 1:1 to host CPUs 0-9, 13 GiB), on radiod's own core
# (vCPU 6, isolcpus=6-9, nohz_full) at the host hookscript's production
# 3.2 GHz pin, with `smd admin wisdom plan --fresh` (fftwf-wisdom -n):
# every one of the 65 profiles measured here, nothing imported from an
# earlier bundle.  The guest cannot see the host's resctrl partition, so
# radiod_l3_bytes is unknown; the plan was measured under whatever share
# the host gives vCPU 6 in production, which is the point.
#
# Covers BOTH RX888 front-end rates: rof1620000 (64.8 Msps) and
# rof3240000 (129.6 Msps), plus the demod channel sizes and the 23
# ka9q-web zoom levels.  Run time 3 h 10 m (2026-10-31 17:45-20:55Z),
# station stopped throughout.
#
# Replaces the 2026-10-02 WB6CXC-7 bundle (302 codelets, bare-metal
# resctrl 5 MiB partition).  Measured right after install on AI6VN-PM:
#   omni  129.6 Msps, 43 channels   fft 96% of its core (was 94-99%)
#   se    129.6 Msps, 34 channels   fft 59%
# so at 129.6 Msps a 5560U vCPU is near saturation with either plan;
# the lever there is 64.8 Msps where the channel set allows it.
#
# Converged: /var/lib/ka9q-radio/fft.log stayed EMPTY across the restart
# that followed the plan.  Harvested from AI6VN-PM 2026-10-31.
